{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions","id":47608,"title":"Benedictions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T14:25:42-08:00","id":47608,"title":"Benedictions?","content":"So Benedictions raise a lot of questions, some of which work fine as in-setting mysteries; but some of which I've been wrestling with from the perspective of setting coherence and conspiracy histories.<br /> <br /> - How did Malleus discover/gain-access to Benedictions?<br /> <br /> - What keeps them solely the territory of Malleus? What's stopping the Catholic Church from performing public resurrections?<br /> <br /> I have some ideas for my own game, a couple of which are based on the fact that the Cainite Heresy doesn't grab me as a whole Conspiracy, but several interesting traits of it are raidable for Malleus (originating from a Blood Cult bound through vitae-tainted Communion fits with the liberated Ghoul at the Conspiracy's head...)<br /> <br /> * Steal how Rites of Denial work. Malleus uses &quot;holy blood&quot; to perform Benedictions. This limited resource keeps access to Benedictions strictly controlled by Cardinal Ambrogio.<br /> <br /> *As above but not as extreme - Benedictions don't use said blood, but before one can wield them there is an ordination ritual of anointment that uses said blood.<br /> <br /> *Not stealing from the Cainite Heresy - the spiritual patrons (Saints?) of Benedictions are who limit access to said rites' miracles - and they're only interested in granting access to Hunters. To thematically enforce this point, I wouldn't let things like Hands of Saint Luke or the Boon of Lazarus work on anyone injured or killed by &quot;natural causes&quot; - they are solely for the Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T15:04:06-08:00","id":47632,"title":"","content":"I'm usually using the last one. The most simple and logical, IMO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T15:28:20-08:00","id":47641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions#post47608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- How did Malleus discover/gain-access to Benedictions?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know the exact details but have a look at the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=13415#post13415\">spoiler here</a> for a hint. Maybe search the books for Padre Ambrogio? (I'd do it but it's late, need sleep).<br /> <br /> I imagine the Vatican's enormous restricted libarary has something to do with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions#post47608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- What keeps them solely the territory of Malleus? What's stopping the Catholic Church from performing public resurrections?</div> </div> </div> </div> Genera conventions, seriously there's no logical reason for it.<br /> <br /> Even if Baudolino has iron fisted control over who gets Benedictions it's in his best interest to publicly spread them across the world. More Catholics means more resources for his personal blood acquisition network.<br /> <br /> Heck, he dosn't really need much. One vampire chained in the basement will be good for decades. A miracle performing Church with medieval level moral authority could easily get away with disappearing a replacement. Feeding patients from a hospital to the vampire under anaesthetic then refilling them with The Hands of St Luke. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions#post47608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some ideas for my own game, a couple of which are based on the fact that the Cainite Heresy doesn't grab me as a whole Conspiracy</div> </div> </div> </div> You too? I see them as a very very large and dangerous compact.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I don't even try to justify it. I just say &quot;genera conventions&quot; and wave my hands furiously. IMO, if everyone agrees to suspend disbelief that's a lot more robust than justifications. That said in my fannon the Longinius / Athanasius conflict is actually a Longinius internal split - I promote the Sisterhood of St. Wisdom to one of the big three and have them secretly spreading benedictions to non-Vigil matters. (That's probably going to show up in Cults, without them being one of the big three)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:27:15-08:00","id":47682,"title":"","content":"I accept genre conventions as guideposts for the setting, but I think actual in-setting explanations can help provide plot hooks - especially with the Conspiracies, as they should have tons of secrets and history to pull on in-game.<br /> <br /> As I'm finishing up KSI's history, I'm just thinking a lot about the other Conspiracies, and I have lists of basically the stuff I'd want to include in &quot;splat-book&quot; (ala the CWoD) length coverage of them. Actually I should start another thread for VALKYRIE on that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:37:42-08:00","id":48301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=47682#post47682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I accept genre conventions as guideposts for the setting, but I think actual in-setting explanations can help provide plot hooks - especially with the Conspiracies, as they should have tons of secrets and history to pull on in-game.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with this in principle, but once you get to the point where the <i>Catholic Church</i> are covering up <i>miracles from God</i>; there's no justification.<br /> <br /> (I don't particularly like the one where Benediction only works for the Vigil, because thelogoically speaking that's clearly not Catholic. I'm ok with ambiguity but not a clear no)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T01:02:13-08:00","id":48790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=48301#post48301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree with this in principle, but once you get to the point where the <i>Catholic Church</i> are covering up <i>miracles from God</i>; there's no justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's &quot;the Church&quot; - then yeah, that makes no sense. If MALLEUS has a good reason to conceal it from the rest of the Church (like a controlled resource that is less holy than they pretend to their lower ranked agents) then there's a good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T06:34:01-08:00","id":48916,"title":"","content":"There's enough people looking at the Catholic Church like it's the Anti-Christ. You introduce Benedictions into the world like a bunch of magicians(particularly since Benedictions have always been implied to be run by something that feels <i>wrong</i> and most certainly not loving God-like) and it's not going to be long before people point out the Devil can perform his own miracles and start looking cross-eyed at the Catholics. It all goes downhill from there.<br /> <br /> Religious people have a tight rope to walk when it comes to the entire miracle thing, and as a general rule a lot of them take the stance of &quot;Faith Precedes the Miracle&quot; seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T08:53:49-08:00","id":49005,"title":"","content":"As a second point, much like man can lick too, things in the shadows have their own miracles. It'd be very easy to lose control over, particularly since some of the shadows tricks are more impressive than benedictions, such as, I dunno, a rain of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T12:04:44-08:00","id":49182,"title":"","content":"Arcane, your first comment makes sense given the weird thought patterns common to WoD mortals but not for regular people. I can't imagine miracles decreasing the Church's popularity, as for Benedictions being implied to be not of gods. There's evidence both ways, like the Feast Days or the Morality bonus. I like it being ambigious.<br /> <br /> Your second comment; I point out that the things in the shadows are already using stuff like that to prove to people that they should join their cults. I suppose you could argue that public acceptance of magic might lead to it being more effective at seeking converts but I think the Church has a fair chance (and the self-confidence to try) at framing it as a theology debate not a power debate. &quot;Yes God doesn't give much power, we can heal, what more do we need? But that guy promising magic gold for everyone, have you even read his so called holy book?!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=48790#post48790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's &quot;the Church&quot; - then yeah, that makes no sense. If MALLEUS has a good reason to conceal it from the rest of the Church (like a controlled resource that is less holy than they pretend to their lower ranked agents) then there's a good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well assuming they could pull the same deception on the Church itself, even if they only gave one guy (the Pope?) a supply that would be worth a lot more in devotion than one extra Hunter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T14:08:57-08:00","id":49289,"title":"","content":"That's not WoD mortals, that's actually people. Think about kids at magic shows-either they are completely invested in it or become more jaded as they observe it. A &quot;Miracle at Demand&quot; sort of thing does much the same-and in fact, the &quot;at Demand&quot; part will do a lot to jade people to it. Running with Christianity here for a second, because why not, even though Jesus did do a lot of miracles, why do you think a vast a majority of his time was actually spent just preaching and talking to people? He often performed miracles at tipping points.<br /> <br /> People are prone to skepticism. Miracles don't build faith, they build a case that two plus two equals four-and what's more, it's two plus two in the hands of man, not some higher being.<br /> <br /> This ties into the second point. Have the Pope go in front of everyone and raise the dead and claim it a miracle from God? Okay. A Changeling who wants to challenge that can arrange his own sort of show, do much the same, and then casually point out &quot;if God's responsible for that, then he's a bastard, cause here's how I can do that&quot;. A Demon willing to risk compromise can do that as well, and if a mage can overcome paradox and disbelief(A stretch), that also works. A Mummy can resurrect someone from the dead and quite frankly go &quot;Praise be the Judges of Duat&quot;. And from there, you start a magical arms races of people who can do this, that, and other. And all the while, there are people looking at this going &quot;Okay, this guy claims it's all God, and this guy is pointing out that it's just really advanced technical application of physics/mystical contracts/applied will&quot;. People will be more prone to the relatable material, and without significant consequences otherwise(most consequences actually balance out to about even, actually), they're going to take their world into their hands, and ta hell with God.<br /> <br /> Some people might be all for trying to counter argue that those magics are lesser or of unsavory sources and shouldn't be used.... which creates an issue when you don't exactly feel like it's God working on you when the Catholics are doing their hoodoo. Lots of people are used to the idea of masks, particularly with charlatan priests and magicians and when actual magic hits the stage, you have no choice but to rely on what you feel. It can have all the saints days benefits and the morality bonuses it wants-magic can wear masks too, like a conman in a frock. At the end of the day, it comes down to individual perception, and Benedictions have regularly been described as having the look of the Christian Divine but feeling...wrong somehow.<br /> <br /> In the middle of this, there is going to be an arms race of bigger and better miracles to prove one is more right than the other, and Benedictions just can't keep up. Vampires and Demons can make it rain blood, Changeling can vastly flood/whiteout/freeze/drought a place quickly, mages do what mages do, and everyone else does their stuff, and Benedictions just can't hold a torch. It'd be a fight, sure, but sooner or later, the elements combine and Catholicism-hell, Catholicism in particular with how unpopular it is-would be crushed.<br /> <br /> From the individual faith of people to the mass rejection of the validity of Catholic power, performing public Benedictions is just inviting the entire downfall of every domino in existence. Miracles will not lead the way for the church because it's too easy to swing in any way. Only Faith can build up the people and power the Church needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T14:18:34-08:00","id":49292,"title":"","content":"@ArcaneArts<br /> <br /> That's really well thought out. I could definitely see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:16:38-08:00","id":49931,"title":"","content":"You start by saying that Jesus only performed miracles at tipping points, who's to say that the Church won't follow Jesus' example? I hear that the church are rather big on Jesus in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next you talk about a magical arms race with two advantages to the non-Catholics. Firstly that everyone else has miracles and secondly that Benediction isn't feel quite right. To the first I will counter that most magic is either:<br /> 1) Highly unethical.<br /> 2) Really really hard to learn.<br /> <br /> Sure a Changeling might be able to bring back the dead (I don't see that Contract, so lets say the Changeling can heal). Well to learn that contract you must first be taken to a horrific realm of torture in Arcadia, and then escape. That's pretty damn hard. To learn Benedictions you must take a training course in the Vatican. Mage's have to Awaken, Sin-Eaters have to die. Vampires have to be vampires and Sons of Phobos power their magic by cutting out hearts. To put it simply, in an arms race the only people in the cannon WoD who can match the MM for magic that can easily be taught are other hunter conspiracies and Vampires. I don't think I need to explain why the public will prefer the Church to Vampires.<br /> <br /> As to your second point. That Benedictions &quot;feel wrong&quot;. What do you think the other magic feels like? Changeling magic is tinged with madness, Supernal magic triggers disbelief in your Soul, Mummies are surrounded by an aura of existential dread. <br /> <br /> <br /> So I think if it came to a maical arms race, the Church will probably win. Of all the magic that is easily taught and doesn't require hideously unethical power sources theirs is the best. The Church ideal is probably one miracle every decade or so, enough to prove the proper skeptics (rationalists, not god haters) that the big guy is real. Enough to get people's attention so they can preach about morality and faith. But if that's not an option and public miracles will inevitably cause a magical arms race; I think that a step up from arguing with Richard Dawkins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally; you're overlooking something really really simple, obvious and important. Who says the Church has to make the first move? What's to stop the Priests of Isis building a big alter in the middle of a public place and get people to form a line for divine healing? Even if the Church doesn't want to fight a miracle war, they should be preparing their defences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:23:52-08:00","id":50073,"title":"","content":"You're going about this in an entirely too rational utilitarian manner. Benedictions aren't a resource to be maximised, they're miracles from God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:57:46-08:00","id":50114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=49931#post49931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to your second point. That Benedictions &quot;feel wrong&quot;. What do you think the other magic feels like? Changeling magic is tinged with madness, Supernal magic triggers disbelief in your Soul, Mummies are surrounded by an aura of existential dread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is part of the point- Benedictions are, according to the MM, miracles from God. They ARE supposed to be different from all other types of &quot;magic&quot;, because they are supposed to have the &quot;right one&quot;. If the other magics feel &quot;wrong&quot;, and Benedictions feel &quot;wrong&quot;, than Benedictions are truly just another type of magic trick instead of a gift from God- which could result at an internal crisis of faith, where even the church doesn't believe itself.<br /> <br /> And if there will be an &quot;arms race&quot; of everyone showing he has better magics, not only that Benediction will be be shown as less powerful, but that internal faith crisis could prove itself fatal- especially that there are other magics with christian aesthetics, and in that case the chances that the vampire with the Thebean Sorcery will draw more followers than the old priest who chant the names of the saints. Something like Moses vs the Egyptian sorcerers, only with the vampire as Moses.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to think on humanity as a rational being. A person is a rational being- humanity is damn stupid, and even more in WoD than in real life. There will be enough people who will support the monsters if they'll talk with them nice enough and pay them enough. There are also enough people who will look at angel in the eyes and claim it isn't real (I know some of those myself). There will be enough people to seek after a &quot;scientific explanation&quot; or even that they would just won't care. In the end, if there will be an arms race, the chances are that the more powerful group will be the one to win the support of the masses.<br /> <br /> tl,dr- Benedictions feeling &quot;wrong&quot; like any other magic is the problem, humanity is stupid, the strong survive and I don't think that the public will prefer the Catholic Church upon the vampiric Church if they are paid enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:09:20-08:00","id":50132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=50073#post50073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going about this in an entirely too rational utilitarian manner. Benedictions aren't a resource to be maximised, they're miracles from God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty as charged. Though I still think that it's implausible that the MM would see these miracles as exclusively for hunting Vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=50114#post50114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that is part of the point- Benedictions are, according to the MM, miracles from God. They ARE supposed to be different from all other types of &quot;magic&quot;, because they are supposed to have the &quot;right one&quot;. If the other magics feel &quot;wrong&quot;, and Benedictions feel &quot;wrong&quot;, than Benedictions are truly just another type of magic trick instead of a gift from God- which could result at an internal crisis of faith, where even the church doesn't believe itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it has four legs does not mean it's a cow. The fact it has common traits with other magic doesn't isn't evidence either way on it's origins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=50114#post50114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if there will be an &quot;arms race&quot; of everyone showing he has better magics, not only that Benediction will be be shown as less powerful, but that internal faith crisis could prove itself fatal- especially that there are other magics with christian aesthetics, and in that case the chances that the vampire with the Thebean Sorcery will draw more followers than the old priest who chant the names of the saints. Something like Moses vs the Egyptian sorcerers, only with the vampire as Moses.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really doubt it. Firstly because even for a powerful vampire elder; going from maybe a dozen rivals and their pawns searching for the bodies in your closet to thousands is a big deal. The Sanctum are not nice people and trying to hide that while under a spot-light 24/7 from the entire of humanity is beyond their talents.<br /> <br /> Secondly because the LeS would support the Church. Converting mortals from Catholothism to LeS? That is, quite literally, heresy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=50114#post50114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl,dr- Benedictions feeling &quot;wrong&quot; like any other magic is the problem, humanity is stupid, the strong survive and I don't think that the public will prefer the Catholic Church upon the vampiric Church if they are paid enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are limits to the stupidity of the general public. Choosing a outright evil vampire because he has more powerful magic goes beyond that limit - and it goes in the outright opposite direction to human stupidity. We're xenophobic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:15:41-08:00","id":50140,"title":"","content":"Maybe God does not want everybody to have miracles? If everyone had Benedictions they wouldn't be miracles anymore, but just another type of magic you can learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T20:16:20-08:00","id":51328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=50140#post50140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe God does not want everybody to have miracles? If everyone had Benedictions they wouldn't be miracles anymore, but just another type of magic you can learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like most of the WoD authors, I do not assume such an entity exists in the setting. It can be an open possibility - but if an explanation RELIES on the existence of God, it's not useful explanation in-setting (outside of a character's beliefs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T20:36:20-08:00","id":51342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=48301#post48301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I don't particularly like the one where Benediction only works for the Vigil, because thelogoically speaking that's clearly not Catholic. I'm o<span style=\"font-family:arial\">k with</span> ambiguity but not a clear no)</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of miracles as spells that can be learned by anyone in a specific organization and reliably called upon to the user's will is in complete contradiction with Catholic doctrine to begin with. Saints can be direct intercessionaries with God, but the best anyone else can do is pray and hope. The idea of &quot;secret knowledge&quot; allowing miracles is an inherently gnostic concept.<br /> <br /> The &quot;saints&quot; that Benedictions call upon facilitating miracles, having a specific purpose they're willing intercede for can be argued to fall under &quot;mysterious ways&quot;. Like Satan tempting Jesus in the desert, miracles are not to be called upon for any purpose other than that which God has <span style=\"font-family:arial\">willed <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 'You shall not put the Lord, your God, to the test.' A point which the Gospels of course reiterate with Jesus refusing to perform miracles to prove his divinity to Pontius Pilate.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T21:22:10-08:00","id":51374,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: Individual Malleus hunters only know that Benedictions are not meant to be publicly shared and get loose doctrinal explanations coached in Jesus not &quot;performing&quot; for Pilate, etc. Higher ups will even come down on those who start laying the Hands of St Luke at local hospitals (individuals uninvolved in the Hunt saved in this manner are often plagued by dreams of them owing their life to God and having a sacred duty to hunt evil now).<br /> <br /> One possible truth is that Ambrogio maintains heretical mystic rituals that facilitate Benedictions and to many wielder relative to the supply of supernatural blood that facilitates said rituals strains the 'miracle' he's facilitating &quot;through the transubstantiation of the blood of satan to the blood of Christ&quot; (as he would explain if revealed to PCs). Obviously its all INSANELY blasphemous, and Ambrogio is the biggest hypocrite on the planet. The magics themselves descend from Mithraist Hunters, his own vampiric patron having conducted experiments with him in one of the Mithraeum beneath Rome. Actual Saints may be involved via spells that once targeted pagan deities now being aimed at them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most Popes have no idea of Malleus' existence. A few in the Curia know enough not to ask further questions. This roughly parallels VALKYRIE's relationship with the President (completely in the dark) and the Joint Chiefs (know enough not to ask further). As a Cardinal Emeritus (over 80) he does not vote in the Curia and has no official duties, so the secret 200th Cardinal attracts little attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T21:44:28-08:00","id":51385,"title":"","content":"Well, time to get back to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=49931#post49931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You start by saying that Jesus only performed miracles at tipping points, who's to say that the Church won't follow Jesus' example? I hear that the church are rather big on Jesus in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe for small affairs, maybe even for something akin to the total of the people on the Mount for Jesus's sermon, with a majority of people who are likely to be swayed. But the question wasn't on small affairs with a controlled demographic, or even the same as having a revival, this is about the Catholic Church doing public miracles. That implies a large scale presentation to the uncontrolled masses. This sets the stage for some big ass problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next you talk about a magical arms race with two advantages to the non-Catholics. Firstly that everyone else has miracles and secondly that Benediction isn't feel quite right. To the first I will counter that most magic is either:<br /> 1) Highly unethical.<br /> 2) Really really hard to learn. </div> </div> </div>Actually, I have a list of four problems that put it in favor of the non-Catholics:<br /> <br /> 1)Everyone has miracles.<br /> 2)Everyone else's miracles are a hell of a lot bigger.<br /> 3)Everyone else's doesn't require God, Jesus, Apostles, or Saints.<br /> 4)Benedictions feel wrong compared to everyone else's.<br /> <br /> Benedictions alone aren't a dog in a fight, unless you count the chihuahua. Of course something is off about a Sin-Eaters manifestations, it's fucking fueled by death(loosely speaking). Of course you feel screwed when a Changeling uses his magic, it's clearly binding on a fated level. Of course a Mummy's power makes you want to piss yourself, it's ancient magic. Even lower end stuff, like the Les Mysteres Rites Du Cheval or the magics of Second Sight, it feels wrong to us, but it feels right given what it is. And a lot of those powers don't come with the strings of God-granted, the the Les Mysteres aren't going to do any better at recruiting, but the Ceremonial Mages and Hedge Witches are.<br /> <br /> But the other people can do so much more and on much bigger scales, and that when your entire power base is on &quot;Look what I can do&quot;, having someone who can one up you hardcore is a bad idea. In the World of Darkness, there is always some like that around. The only argument you have is that your cards come from God, and when it doesn't feel like God, it sure loses validity. Benedictions alone are bad case of magic to whip out into the open.<br /> <br /> So, your two arguments.<br /> <br /> 1)Tell that to Ceremonial and Hedge Magic, actually. Not as big, but certainly more diverse, feels right for what it is, and is something more in your hands. THere's a lot more out there than just this.<br /> 2)Maybe, but most of the low hanging fruit for humans isn't necessarily any harder to learn than Benedictions<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure a Changeling might be able to bring back the dead (I don't see that Contract, so lets say the Changeling can heal). Well to learn that contract you must first be taken to a horrific realm of torture in Arcadia, and then escape. That's pretty damn hard. To learn Benedictions you must take a training course in the Vatican. Mage's have to Awaken, Sin-Eaters have to die. Vampires have to be vampires and Sons of Phobos power their magic by cutting out hearts. To put it simply, in an arms race the only people in the cannon WoD who can match the MM for magic that can easily be taught are other hunter conspiracies and Vampires. I don't think I need to explain why the public will prefer the Church to Vampires. </div> </div> </div>Yes, no one wants to sign up for the summer camp in Arcadia(Well, maybe the extremely militant, heh)-but first of all, let's put aside learning it and just go with who's going to listen to who. Catholics raise the dead, Changeling raises the dead and then makes it snow in Florida. Catholics...scratch their head.<br /> <br /> Or, with vampires, that conveniently have a God oriented covenant(Who, admittedly, will be fighting the Ordo and the Circle in this hypothetical at the same time as everything else), let's go this angle: Yes, I am a vampire, but! 1)Anything he can do, I can do better. 2) I also serve God(and I'll ignore the details of my service for now) and seek to do 'good', and 3)Just like your pop-cultural heroes! 4)Oh, by the way, these miracles are tailored to my curse, which is why it looks like/acts like/feels like this.<br /> <br /> Yes, people can be xenophobic, and yes, lots of people will choose the Church over the vampires on principle-but a lot more people are going to be right there on the fence than makes either side comfortable. It's wouldn't be a landslide victory for the Catholics or the vampires-that's why neither side does it. If the Catholics thought they could end the Vigil by doing it publicly, they would(and they did, and a fair number of accounts mentioned how troublesome that was for everything),and if vampires thought they could, they would. It's not a landslide it's a war waiting to happen,which neither wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to your second point. That Benedictions &quot;feel wrong&quot;. What do you think the other magic feels like? Changeling magic is tinged with madness, Supernal magic triggers disbelief in your Soul, Mummies are surrounded by an aura of existential dread. </div> </div> </div>All of which feels appropriate to the sources these things are attributed, as opposed to conman-in-the-frock magic of Benediction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I think if it came to a maical arms race, the Church will probably win. Of all the magic that is easily taught and doesn't require hideously unethical power sources theirs is the best. The Church ideal is probably one miracle every decade or so, enough to prove the proper skeptics (rationalists, not god haters) that the big guy is real. Enough to get people's attention so they can preach about morality and faith. But if that's not an option and public miracles will inevitably cause a magical arms race; I think that a step up from arguing with Richard Dawkins. </div> </div> </div>The Catholics only have one advantage, and that is, as we like to discuss with humanity versus monsters in general, sheer numbers. Roman Catholicism, granted, has numbers in the millions(1.2 billion people, actually), and while most of them seem to be in the &quot;I'm Catholic because my pappy was Catholic&quot; camp, that's not a ringing endorsement.<br /> <br /> But putting that aside, there's a reason it hasn't been done large scale in the open-because the Church <i>wouldn't</i> win. It'd be a very messy battle of factors rather than anything clear cut. That's why it hasn't been done yet(among a myriad of other reasons, granted-I expect the Church is somewhat aware of the things the monsters keep off the doorstep by being there as well, much like I expect many of the Conspiracies to actually know and not fuck with, but that's another subject). They don't want to push the button on a move that isn't a guarenteed win<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally; you're overlooking something really really simple, obvious and important. Who says the Church has to make the first move? What's to stop the Priests of Isis building a big alter in the middle of a public place and get people to form a line for divine healing? Even if the Church doesn't want to fight a miracle war, they should be preparing their defenses. </div> </div> </div>Well, two reasons. One is that no one wants to be the guy who pushed the button. That entire subject is basically an the result of nuclear deterrent-the first one to make the push these days is the one who might end the world. No one wants to be that guy. The second is also the fact that many of these people have other fish to fry. Mages don't want to usher in the Abyss, changelings would really like it if no one invited the Strangers en masse, demons are quite fine with where the God Machine's focus is at, thank you very much, mummies just don't have the time, etc. Add in that humanity creates a sort of buffer zone(yes, even against the Strix, which you think wouldn't matter but it does) against these guys and now really no one wants to push the issue.<br /> <br /> It's a big issue-bigger than most characters we play as can really deal with. Status quo is God(heh heh, I'm funny) for a reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T23:13:28-08:00","id":51425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions#post47608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - What keeps them solely the territory of Malleus? What's stopping the Catholic Church from performing public resurrections?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We have powers granted to raise the dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Congrats, what have you been using them on for the last thousand years or so?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, capturing and draining vampire blood to serve our leader&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;....&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing to remember is the lip service that most hunter organizations give on the question of &quot;why do we operate in the shadows?&quot; is to &quot;protect the public&quot;. That is somewhat legit but the other one is to do so is to admit that one has been using all these fancy powers to injure, hurt, and sometimes, outright kill people.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T23:18:11-08:00","id":51428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51425#post51425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;We have powers granted to raise the dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Congrats, what have you been using them on for the last thousand years or so?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, capturing and draining vampire blood to serve our leader&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;....&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing to remember is the lip service that most hunter organizations give on the question of &quot;why do we operate in the shadows?&quot; is to &quot;protect the public&quot;. That is somewhat legit but the other one is to do so is to admit that one has been using all these fancy powers to injure, hurt, and sometimes, outright kill people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they need to tell people that? I mean why would a priest preforming miracles need to tell people anything about Malleus at all?<br /> <br /> Hell, 99.9999999% of Malleus members don't know about the feeding vampires to Ambrogio thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T23:49:25-08:00","id":51437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51328#post51328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like most of the WoD authors, I do not assume such an entity exists in the setting. It can be an open possibility - but if an explanation RELIES on the existence of God, it's not useful explanation in-setting (outside of a character's beliefs).</div> </div> </div> </div>I also do not assume the Christian God exists in the setting, but there still is a possibility that there are entities that are responsible for the &quot;magic&quot; of the Maleus Malificarum. Most magic in the world of darkness comes from somewhere. These entities (the saints?) could for example be the spirit gods of the Vatican.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T01:38:18-08:00","id":51478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51437#post51437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also do not assume the Christian God exists in the setting, but there still is a possibility that there are entities that are responsible for the &quot;magic&quot; of the Maleus Malificarum. Most magic in the world of darkness comes from somewhere. These entities (the saints?) could for example be the spirit gods of the Vatican.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that said benefactors won't grant Benedictions to anyone else outside of Malleus? Or that they won't interceed to allow the miracles in other contexts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T02:27:33-08:00","id":51494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51478#post51478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying that said benefactors won't grant Benedictions to anyone else outside of Malleus? Or that they won't interceed to allow the miracles in other contexts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are equally valid (but I prefer the second).<br /> <br /> I'd say those entities support the entire Catholic church, instead of just Maleus, as Maleus is too small to attract such strong attention. These entities grant miracles to those who need them most (and won't abuse them), because that is where the most faith is generated. Because of the lifestyle of hunters they make the ideal candidates to perform these miracles for, but that doesn't mean catholic priests couldn't use them, I someone tought them and they needed some extra light in this dark world.<br /> <br /> In my opinion a spirit court of these &quot;Saints&quot; would make a interesting addition to the vatican.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 01-17-2014, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:57:03-08:00","id":51806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51342#post51342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of miracles as spells that can be learned by anyone in a specific organization and reliably called upon to the user's will is in complete contradiction with Catholic doctrine to begin with. Saints can be direct intercessionaries with God, but the best anyone else can do is pray and hope. The idea of &quot;secret knowledge&quot; allowing miracles is an inherently gnostic concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>To explain this I'm going to turn to a variant of the <a href=\"http://www.speculativefictionstories.com/biglie\" target=\"_blank\">one big lie</a> concept. That a story can tell one big lie and everything else must follow logically from that one big lie. If you focus purely on the MM that big lie is &quot;the church has a secret militant wing who hunt monsters with guns and magic that might or might not come from God via the saints&quot;. This interpreation is clearly is supported by the books, there are hints that Benedictions might not be as holy as the MM believes, and there's hints that they might be genuine like the morality bonus.<br /> <br /> So when you point out that Catholic doctrine contradicts the rules for Benedictions, that doesn't matter so much because that's covered by the one big lie. In the WoD, clearly catholic doctrine must have room for this because Benedictions exist and it's explicitly a possibility that they might be genuinely from god. Just like in the WoD the laws of reality must allow for vampires and magic prayers to exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51385#post51385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is about the Catholic Church doing public miracles. That implies a large scale presentation to the uncontrolled masses. This sets the stage for some big ass problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says who? There's absolutely no reason why the MM couldn't have a policy of only the Pope does public miracles. Or perform one Resurrection and pretend that it was god without any mortal using the secret prayer. <br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is at heart the fact that it's implausible that the MM hasn't tried to use Benedictions to put bums in pews. Everything else is just window dressing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51385#post51385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course something is off about a Sin-Eaters manifestations, it's fucking fueled by death(loosely speaking). Of course you feel screwed when a Changeling uses his magic, it's clearly binding on a fated level. Of course a Mummy's power makes you want to piss yourself, it's ancient magic. Even lower end stuff, like the Les Mysteres Rites Du Cheval or the magics of Second Sight, it feels wrong to us, but it feels right given what it is. And a lot of those powers don't come with the strings of God-granted, the the Les Mysteres aren't going to do any better at recruiting, but the Ceremonial Mages and Hedge Witches are.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is that the other kinds of magic feel as bad/worse than Benedictions, but because no one claimed they weren't bad to begin with they'll be seen as superior to Benediction. I don't buy it one bit. <br /> <br /> Firstly there's precedent in the scripture for magic feeling scary; <b><i>Be Not Afraid</i></b>. Secondly I think that the absolute value of the magic's feelings matters far more than the relative value of it's expectations. Benedictions don't feel that terrible, take this bit from The Fortitude of St George. &quot;Tradition holds this to be the gaze of St. George, but some have described the presence as vaguely...other.&quot; Note the word vaguely, on an absolute scale that's not so horrible. I think people are going to massively prefer magic that feels &quot;vaguely other&quot; for no known reason to &quot;blasts you with the feeling of an ancient inescapable horror&quot; that can be easily explained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51385#post51385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that when your entire power base is on &quot;Look what I can do&quot;, having someone who can one up you hardcore is a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> And where do you get this idea that anyone's going to make their entire power base on look what I can do?<br /> <br /> &quot;Look! here's solid evidence that God exists. No it's not proof and there's all those other magic types but doesn't God seem more plausible in a world with lots of magic? Whether control, why would we need to do that, healing should be enough for anyone. Now lets get back to talking about important stuff like faith, morality and getting your souls into heaven&quot;. Seems like a reasonable strategy to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51385#post51385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Tell that to Ceremonial and Hedge Magic, actually. Not as big, but certainly more diverse, feels right for what it is, and is something more in your hands. THere's a lot more out there than just this.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a fair argument that Benediction really is just Ceremonial Magic under a different set of mechanics. Certainly it matches them for diversity and exceeds them in power, just compare The Hands of St Luke to the Healing ritual.<br /> <br /> There's also an explicit possibility in Second Sight that either of those might be as hard as a combination of computer programming and Olympian athletics; Benediction is explicitly easy enough for a construction worker to learn in-between fighting vampires, working construction, and hiding his double life. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51385#post51385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)Maybe, but most of the low hanging fruit for humans isn't necessarily any harder to learn than Benedictions</div> </div> </div> </div> As of yet, I've not seen a single cannon low hanging fruit that's more powerful than Benediction without being powered by horrible ethical compromises.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the end there isn't a single cannon group in the WoD who have the resources and influence of the Catholic Church in possession of a magic system that can be taught to anyone. If it came down to a &quot;who' magic is best&quot; fight that infrastructure is their advantage. Other groups might have flashier powers, but none of them can provide the healer in every parish that the MM can.<br /> <br /> In practice though I doubt the Church would ever say that you should follow them purely because they have the best magic. That just doesn't fit their MO. They're far more likely to follow Jesus' example and use Miracles to get people's attention so they can preach scripture and morality. One thing the Church has never lacked is good apologetics and theologians, I think that however the Church chooses to spin it they'll at least come up with a competent message. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51385#post51385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, two reasons. One is that no one wants to be the guy who pushed the button. That entire subject is basically an the result of nuclear deterrent-the first one to make the push these days is the one who might end the world.</div> </div> </div> </div> The question I have to ask here, is how did that deterrent ever get put in the box? That's the elephant in the room for most urban fantasies.<br /> <br /> Why has no Sin-Eater gone public and created their own cult? Sin-Eater culture is too diffused and organised to prevent every occurrence. What happened to all the ancient heroes who bound a True Fae in Pledges to be a benevolent protective deity? Basically how did the Masqurade start?<br /> <br /> This is why I say it's down to convention and best that you don't try justifying it. There's really no justification that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T18:03:14-08:00","id":52019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=51428#post51428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they need to tell people that? I mean why would a priest preforming miracles need to tell people anything about Malleus at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people preforming real life miracles tends to bring out people who act questions. media, reporters, etc and now you're dealing a bunch of people hounding you from the ends of the earth while you are trying to do your job which happens to be killing people.<br /> <br /> You have the powers of God and you are using them to burn people alive. Surely you can see how this can be a very bad thing should it turn public.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T21:03:35-08:00","id":52122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47608-benedictions?p=52019#post52019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because people preforming real life miracles tends to bring out people who act questions. media, reporters, etc and now you're dealing a bunch of people hounding you from the ends of the earth while you are trying to do your job which happens to be killing people.<br /> <br /> You have the powers of God and you are using them to burn people alive. Surely you can see how this can be a very bad thing should it turn public.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... again - why would a wielder of Benedictions have to care about the Hunt when they can walk into a hospital and perform holy miracles to raise the dead? What ties wielding Benedictions to the Hunt when you've got magics like the Hands of Saint Luke and Lazarus' Boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T00:43:00-08:00","id":52202,"title":"","content":"I'm with Glamourweaver here. The average parish priest doesn't know about the MM, why should the average hospital priest in the Order of Saint Luke know about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}